pve-wdcbalancer (0.4.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * state.json is updated under the cluster lock by passes, apply tasks and
    dismissals alike: Run now during an apply keeps the apply marker, and
    moves and dismissals made while a pass runs are kept.
  * Apply tasks write a heartbeat; a task whose node is offline, whose
    process is gone or whose heartbeat stopped no longer blocks passes.
  * Circuit breaker: automation pauses after repeated failed moves (fault,
    notification); resume with the GUI or 'wdcbalancer resume'.
  * Holds: nothing is recommended without quorum; only mandatory moves while
    the online nodes settle after a change or usage data is missing.
  * Each move is checked on live data first: quorum, target not in
    maintenance mode, the guest's memory free on the target.
  * Less churn: a fixed cost per migration, a higher cost for moving a guest
    back where it came from, and a tolerated imbalance per threshold.
  * One recommendation per guest and pass; keep-together fixes gather the
    guests on the best node.
  * Rule validation catches keep-together rules that, through a shared VM,
    conflict with a separate rule.
  * Fault notifications are keyed by fault, not message text; the history
    has a size limit; config.json has a schema version.

 -- pve-wdcbalancer maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 23:30:00 +0000

pve-wdcbalancer (0.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Maintenance mode per node (Datacenter > Load Balancing > Maintenance,
    Node > Load Balancing, wdcbalancer maintenance): running guests are
    moved off now, HA guests through HA node maintenance, optionally the
    stopped ones too; what cannot move is reported. Nothing is placed on a
    node in maintenance.
  * Power On (balanced): stopped guests are started on the best node, moved
    there offline first; with manual automation the placement is shown to
    pick from. HA guests are started through HA.
  * Stopped guests are moved offline (on shared storage only the config).

 -- pve-wdcbalancer maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 22:23:22 +0000

pve-wdcbalancer (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Recommendations can be applied: live migration for VMs, restart
    migration for containers, HA migration for HA guests, in a task with
    up to max_concurrent moves per node. Each move is checked again just
    before it starts.
  * Automation levels: with full automation the timer applies the
    recommendations within the threshold; per-VM overrides (disabled,
    manual, partial, full) and the container setting are honoured. No
    moves while Proxmox CRS auto-rebalancing is on.
  * Rules are mirrored into native HA rules for HA guests (node-affinity
    and resource-affinity, named wdcb-<rule>); hand-made HA rules are
    never touched.
  * Notifications for new faults and moves; move history with results.
  * CLI: apply, ha-sync; readable times in history.

 -- pve-wdcbalancer maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 22:12:02 +0000

pve-wdcbalancer (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First release: cluster load balancing that recommends moves.
    Scores every guest (CPU and memory demand from usage and pressure),
    recommends live migrations with priority and reason for maintenance,
    rule violations and load balancing (migration threshold 1-5), with VM
    and host groups, VM/Host must/should rules, keep-together and
    keep-apart rules, per-VM overrides, a placement explanation per guest,
    the Datacenter > Load Balancing panel, the wdcbalancer CLI and a REST
    API. Nothing is moved automatically yet.

 -- pve-wdcbalancer maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 21:27:24 +0000
